course: dictionary
lesson: 9517
title: Stiffly: one word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Stiffly» is an adverb. It tells you how something is done. It has two main meanings: in a stiff way, where a body does not bend easily, and in a cold, formal, unfriendly way. Context tells you which meaning fits.
explain: «After the long walk, Sam climbed the stairs stiffly.» His legs are sore, so stiffly means without bending easily. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «“Thank you,” she answered stiffly.» Nobody's body is stiff here. The word tells you her voice was cold and not friendly, so she may be annoyed. Words like this show feelings as well as actions.
fact: Stiffly means in a stiff way, without bending easily.
fact: Stiffly can also mean in a cold, formal, unfriendly way.
fact: «Walk stiffly» often shows someone is hurt, old, tired or nervous.
fact: «Reply stiffly» often shows the speaker is annoyed or not friendly.
fact: In PE and science, stiffly can describe joints and muscles that do not move freely.
exercise: «The old man got out of his chair stiffly, as his knees were sore.» What does stiffly mean here? | Very loudly | *Without bending easily, because his knees were sore | Wearing a hat | Quickly and happily
exercise: «“Fine,” she said stiffly, and looked away.» What does stiffly suggest? | Sleepy | Excited and full of joy | *Cold and unfriendly | Wet and muddy
exercise: A frightened dog may hold its ears «stiffly forward». What can this mean? | The dog is wet from the rain | *The dog is on alert | The dog is hungry for dinner | The dog is asleep
test: «He shook hands stiffly with the new teacher and did not smile.» What does stiffly show? | Very fast | Covered in mud | Happy and warm | *Cold and unfriendly, not warm
test: «The robot moved stiffly across the floor, like a toy with rusty joints.» What does stiffly mean? | Happily, with a song | Under the water | *Without bending easily, as if its joints are stuck | Very quickly and smoothly
exam: «The guard nodded stiffly and said nothing more.» What does stiffly suggest? | Dancing in the rain | Hungry and tired | Happy to see you | *Cold and formal, not friendly
